## Commands

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `pnpm verify` | Before saying "done" (changed packages only; `--all` for everything); runs automatically before every push |
| `pnpm doctor` | Harness health; `--brief` for where we are and what's next |
| `pnpm lint` · `pnpm typecheck` · `pnpm test` · `pnpm build` · `pnpm e2e` | One gate at a time |
| `pnpm format` | Before committing |
{%- for app in apps %}
| `pnpm dev:{{ app }}` | Run {{ app }} locally |
{%- endfor %}

## The non-negotiables (full list and enforcers in rules.toml)

1. Never commit secrets or `.env` files; never edit an applied migration.
2. Never bypass a gate: no `--no-verify`, no force-push, no disabling tests.
3. `git fetch && git rebase origin/main` before pushing — other agents merge in parallel.
4. Unknown facts become gaps with an owner and a question, never plausible defaults.
5. Colours only from `ui-tokens`; visible text only through `t()` in every locale; API responses
   only through schemas in `packages/shared`; TypeScript strict, no `any`.
6. A story is done when the verifier says so, with evidence, and every scenario has a test citing
   `<ID>.S<n>`. The builder never grades its own work (`/keelokit:build`).
7. Production deploys, money, legal and data deletion wait for the human's yes.

## Changing the rules

A rule without a check is a wish. To add one: write it in `.keelokit/rules.local.toml` with the
test, lint rule, hook or CI job that enforces it. To break one temporarily: add an entry to
`.keelokit/exceptions.toml` with reason, approver and expiry. `pnpm doctor` checks both.
